{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310694,"nonce":"def5Jy7R651XdlBtjoK5qOX/xY8=","title":"tools/llama-diff/compare.sh divergence on haiku/Hamlet prompts vs llama.cpp is PRE-EXISTING sampler-config mismatch (rayzor's ...","message":"**Status: ROOT-CAUSED, pre-existing, NOT a SDOT bug.**\n\nWhen `tools/llama-diff/compare.sh` is run against llama.cpp on prompts other than \"What is the capital of France?\":\n\n- `Write a haiku about the moon.` — diverges after shared prefix\n- `Summarize the plot of Hamlet in one sentence.` — shared prefix \"The play Hamlet, written by William Shakespeare,\" then \"revolves around\" (llama.cpp) vs \"tells the story of\" (rayzor)\n- `What is the capital of France?` — **MATCHes byte-for-byte**\n\nThe remediation workflow `wz8f59bw8` Phase 1 (div agent) verified this divergence:\n1. **Reproduces on pre-SDOT HEAD** with `quant.rs` stashed and release rebuilt → divergence not caused by the SDOT spec-shape PR.\n2. **Byte-identical under `RAYZOR_USE_SDOT=0` and `=1`** on current HEAD → numerical SDOT path is not the discriminator.\n\n**Root cause**: harness sampler-config mismatch in `tools/llama-diff/compare.sh`.\n\n- llama.cpp side: `--temp 0` (true argmax)\n- rayzor side: `nue/examples/llama-chat/Main.hx` maps `temperature=0.01` to `LocalTempSampler(0.01, rep_penalty=1.15, topK=50, seed=42)`\n\nThe 1.15 repetition penalty divides recent-ring-token logits by 1.15. This is a **structural argmax shift, not numerical noise**:\n\n- Paris matches because top-1 dominates top-2 by \u003e log(1.15) ≈ 0.14 — penalty can't flip the argmax\n- Haiku / Hamlet have smaller top-1/top-2 gaps AND tokens that repeat enough to trip the rep ring → penalty flips argmax\n\n**Why this matters**: any earlier \"byte-for-byte multi-prompt MATCH\" memo (e.g. the prior `bugs_rope_interleaved_for_gguf` 71bff00 validation) was either against a different sampler config OR was true at the time and broke when the LocalTempSampler was introduced. Need to be careful with multi-prompt validation claims — only Paris-prompt MATCH is currently load-bearing.\n\n**Fix paths** (in `nue/examples/llama-chat/Main.hx`):\n\n1. **Parametrise LocalTempSampler to skip rep-penalty when temperature ≤ 0.01** — preserves the chat-time UX (temperature ~0 = greedy) but matches llama.cpp's `--temp 0` behaviour for the diff harness.\n2. **Fix the chat-template SIGSEGV** that prevents `temperature=0.0 → ArgmaxSampler` (per `project_llama_chat_temperature_penalty` memo). The reason temperature=0.01 was chosen was because 0.0 hit a trap-stub cascade — root-causing that would let the harness use true argmax.\n3. **Change the bench/compare harness** to pass `--repeat-penalty 1.15` to llama.cpp so both sides use the same sampler config. Probably the cleanest one-shot fix for validation purposes.\n\n**Out of scope for the SDOT spec-shape PR** (`327fd80`). Tracked here for the next sampler-touching workflow.\n\nRelated: [[project-sdot-qmatmul]], [[project-llama-chat-temperature-penalty]] (the LocalTempSampler that injects the rep penalty), [[bugs-rope-interleaved-for-gguf]] (the earlier multi-prompt match claim, likely now stale).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_sdot_multi_prompt_validation_gap` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}